    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L09-ACTIVITY-002",
      "SourceSection": "9.1: Selecting Samples",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Diego has a jar containing 36 coins. Select a coin by using the applet to generate a pair of numbers: one number for the row in the table and a second number for the column. For example, rolling a 3 and then a 5 would mean choosing the…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l09.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L09-ACTIVITY-003",
      "SourceSection": "9.1: Selecting Samples",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Find the mean date for the sample of 5 coins.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l09.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L09-ACTIVITY-004",
      "SourceSection": "9.1: Selecting Samples",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Find the proportion of the sample of 5 coins that were minted in Denver.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l09.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L09-ACTIVITY-005",
      "SourceSection": "9.1: Selecting Samples",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Repeat the process to find 2 more samples of 5 coins, then compute the mean date and proportion that were minted in Denver.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l09.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L09-ACTIVITY-006",
      "SourceSection": "9.2: Examining Sample Statistics",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Use the data from the warm-up to answer the questions.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l09.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L09-ACTIVITY-007",
      "SourceSection": "9.2: Examining Sample Statistics",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Not all the samples have the same mean and proportion. Why not?",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l09.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L09-ACTIVITY-008",
      "SourceSection": "9.2: Examining Sample Statistics",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Examine the histogram for the mean year of coins from the samples. What do you notice?",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l09.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L09-ACTIVITY-009",
      "SourceSection": "9.2: Examining Sample Statistics",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Based on the mean years from the samples, estimate the mean year for all the coins in Diego’s jar. Explain your reasoning.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l09.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L09-ACTIVITY-010",
      "SourceSection": "9.2: Examining Sample Statistics",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Examine the histogram of the proportion of coins in each sample that were minted in Denver. What do you notice?",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l09.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L09-ACTIVITY-011",
      "SourceSection": "9.2: Examining Sample Statistics",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Based on the sample proportions found by the class, estimate the proportion of coins minted in Denver for all the coins in Diego’s jar. Explain your reasoning.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l09.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L09-ACTIVITY-012",
      "SourceSection": "9.3: Variability of Sample Estimates",
      "SourceExcerpt": "A political campaign sends volunteers out into the various parts of the state to get a sense of how well their candidate will do in an upcoming election. Thirty volunteers each get a random sample of 10 people in the state and find the…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l09.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L09-ACTIVITY-013",
      "SourceSection": "9.3: Variability of Sample Estimates",
      "SourceExcerpt": "The mean of these sample proportions is 0.55, and the standard deviation is 0.15.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l09.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L09-ACTIVITY-014",
      "SourceSection": "9.3: Variability of Sample Estimates",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Recall that, for normally distributed data, about 95% of the data is within 2 standard deviations of the mean. What percentage of sample proportions are within 2 standard deviations of the mean for these data? Does this match what we…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l09.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L09-ACTIVITY-015",
      "SourceSection": "9.3: Variability of Sample Estimates",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Estimates for population characteristics are usually given along with a margin of error. The margin of error is the maximum expected difference between the estimate of the population characteristic and the actual population characteristic.…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l09.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L09-ACTIVITY-016",
      "SourceSection": "9.3: Variability of Sample Estimates",
      "SourceExcerpt": "The margin of error we constructed here was constructed at a 95% confidence level. Since 95% of the time our sample proportion is within 2 standard deviations of the true proportion for the population, by using a margin of error of 2…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l09.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L09-ACTIVITY-017",
      "SourceSection": "9.3: Variability of Sample Estimates",
      "SourceExcerpt": "What would happen to the margin of error if we were okay with only capturing the true proportion 90% of the time?",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l09.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L09-ACTIVITY-018",
      "SourceSection": "9.3: Variability of Sample Estimates",
      "SourceExcerpt": "What would happen to the margin of error if needed to capture the true proportion 99% of the time?",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l09.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L09-ACTIVITY-019",
      "SourceSection": "9.3: Variability of Sample Estimates",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Why might someone choose a different confidence level?",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l09.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L09-ACTIVITY-020",
      "SourceSection": "9.3: Variability of Sample Estimates",
      "SourceExcerpt": "In many cases, it is difficult to collect data from an entire population, so using data from a small subset of the larger group is needed. The trade-off is that the incomplete information from such samples can only provide estimates of…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l09.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L09-ACTIVITY-021",
      "SourceSection": "9.3: Variability of Sample Estimates",
      "SourceExcerpt": "For example, a researcher may wish to know how many fish of each type are present in a lake. It would be hard to collect all the fish in the pond to know all of the information, so a small group of fish might be caught to estimate the…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l09.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L09-ACTIVITY-022",
      "SourceSection": "9.3: Variability of Sample Estimates",
      "SourceExcerpt": "To understand how varied the lake's fish are, the researcher may want to take several samples of fish from the lake. After taking many samples of fish, the researcher may find that the number of bass in a sample ranges from 2 to 20 and the…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l09.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L09-ACTIVITY-023",
      "SourceSection": "9.3: Variability of Sample Estimates",
      "SourceExcerpt": "To give a sense of the variability and confidence in estimates, a margin of error is usually given along with the estimate. A margin of error is the maximum expected difference between an estimate for a population characteristic and the…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l09.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L09-ACTIVITY-024",
      "SourceSection": "9.3: Variability of Sample Estimates",
      "SourceExcerpt": "From the fish example, the researcher may use the sample to estimate that there are 800 bass in the lake with a margin of error of 300 bass. This means that the researcher is fairly confident that the number of bass in the lake is…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l09.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U07-L09-ACTIVITY-025",
      "SourceSection": "9.3: Variability of Sample Estimates",
      "SourceExcerpt": "The maximum expected difference between an estimate for a population characteristic and the actual value of the population characteristic.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u07-l09.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
